From: ScorchDroid <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: the remaining sound hooks

Upstream plays sounds from ten places in src/common, every one inside a
client-only block this build compiles out. Patch 0006 hooked two of them
(SoundAction and Explosion) and the other eight stayed silent: the shot
being fired, shield hits, shield/parachute/battery activation, the tank
driving, teleports, lightning and napalm. A parity review found them, and
this patch, together with additions to 0011/0014/0015 for the files those
already own, raises each as a sound event exactly as 0006 does.

Each hook mirrors upstream's own gate - the same "none" check on the sound
name, the same tank-state check on a teleport - and takes the file from the
same accessory field, so a mod's sounds come through too. The one deliberate
difference is the drive: upstream starts a looping source for the whole
movement, and the event queue is one-shot, so the drive gets its sound once
as it sets off.

No !getServerMode() guards, for the reason patches/scorched3d/README.md
records: this port runs these actions on the server context, and the guard
would only switch the sound off.

No game logic changes.

diff --git a/src/common/simactions/PlayMovesSimAction.cpp b/src/common/simactions/PlayMovesSimAction.cpp
index 58e3c6d6..a7ea4f43 100644
--- a/src/common/simactions/PlayMovesSimAction.cpp
+++ b/src/common/simactions/PlayMovesSimAction.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@
 ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 
 #include <simactions/PlayMovesSimAction.hpp>
+#ifdef S3D_SERVER
+	// Android build: sound is raised as an event - see SoundEventQueue.h.
+	#include <SoundEventQueue.h>
+#endif
 #include <engine/ActionController.hpp>
 #include <weapons/AccessoryStore.hpp>
 #include <tanket/TanketAccessories.hpp>
@@ -243,6 +247,17 @@ void PlayMovesSimAction::tankFired(ScorchedContext &context,
 				firedSound, tanket->getLife().getTargetPosition().asVector());
 		}
 	}
+#else
+	// Android build: the weapon's own firing sound, raised as an event. No
+	// !getServerMode() guard - this port runs these actions on the server
+	// context alone, and the guard would only switch the sound off (see
+	// patches/scorched3d/README.md).
+	if (weapon->getParent()->getActivationSound() &&
+		0 != strcmp("none", weapon->getParent()->getActivationSound()))
+	{
+		ScorchDroidAudio::pushSoundEvent(S3D::getModFile(S3D::formatStringBuffer(
+			"data/wav/%s", weapon->getParent()->getActivationSound())));
+	}
 #endif // #ifndef S3D_SERVER
 
 	// Get firing context
